-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",65,{
[2049]="7001B9B9\n1\tTalk to Gadaric Munce at The Forsaken Inn\tRide Candaith's horse or make your way on foot to The Forsaken Inn on the border of the Midgewater Marsh and the Lone-lands along the Great East Road. Candaith thanked you for your assistance and warned that the Eglain must be made to understand that your intentions are just before they will allow you an audience with Radagast the Brown.\n2\tFind and speak with a member of the Eglain in The Forsaken Inn or their camp in Nain Enidh\tFind a member of the Eglain and ask him for the whereabouts of Radagast the Brown. You have worked long and hard to obtain the trust of the Eglain. Now, you must ask them the whereabouts of Radagast the Brown.\n",
[2050]="70041328\n1\tFlat stones can be found at several locations to the west of the Gilrain, in Dor-en-Ernil, south-east of Roamingstar. Roamingstar has given you a number of pebbles to leave on flat stones west of the Gilrain, south of her waterfall glade.\t\n2\tTalk to Roamingstar by the banks of Gilrain\tRoamingstar is waiting for you to return from the errand on which she sent you.\n3\tTalk to Roniel on the banks of the Gilrain\tRoniel has awoken, and you should speak to her and ensure that she is all right.\n4\tTalk to Mornil in Linhir\tRoniel's mother Mornil is back in the town of Linhir, in Dor-en-Ernil. She is by the fountain in the north-east court of Linhir. You have found the missing child and sent her back to her mother.\n5\tTalk to Roniel in Linhir\tRoniel has returned to Linhir, but her mother Mornil does not believe her story.\n6\tTalk to Ingalad in Linhir\tYou have returned Roniel safely to Linhir, and should tell Ingalad of your success.\n",
[2051]="70061C16\n1\tTalk to Meneldir inside Crossway House\tMeneldir is inside Crossway House. You should return to Meneldir and tell him what you learned from Aberthol.\n2\tCollect choice cuts of meat from animals in Sedgemead (total: 10)\030Collect firewood in Sedgemead (total: 8)\030Talk to Bledri inside his home\030Talk to Aldyth inside her home\030Talk to Linnet by the fountain in the northern part of Herne\tMeneldir suggested that you and your companions hunt the animals of Sedgemead for meat, collect firewood for the town braziers, and tell the folk of Herne to gather for the night behind the safe walls of Crossway House.\n3\tRefill town braziers near Crossway House with firewood (total: 8)\tBraziers can be found in front of Crossway House in the town of Herne, waiting for you and your companions to fill them with firewood. Meneldir hopes to keep at bay the evils that threaten Herne by keeping the town braziers lit all night.\n4\tTalk to Meneldir inside Crossway House\tMeneldir is inside Crossway House, waiting to hear about the town's preparations for the approaching night.\n5\tTalk to Meneldir inside Crossway House and wait for night to fall\tMeneldir is inside Crossway House. The preparations have been completed, and night approaches.\n6\tTalk to Meneldir outside Crossway House\tMeneldir stands outside Crossway House after the events of the long night.\n",
[2052]="70061C18\n1\tCollect tarnished jewellery left by the wights (total: 3)\030Collect rusted blades left by the wights (total: 4)\tMeneldir thinks you should clean up the evidence of the wight attack on Herne, to help ease the minds and fears of the townsfolk.\n2\tMeneldir thinks you should clean up the evidence of the wight attack on Herne, to help ease the minds and fears of the townsfolk.\t\n3\tBring the discarded equipment to Meneldir in Herne\tMeneldir stands in the town of Herne, turning the events of the night over and over in his mind.\n4\tTalk to Boromir outside Crossway House in Herne\tBoromir stands in Herne, disgusted by the dead that walk and the events of the previous night.\n5\tTalk to Meneldir outside Crossway House in Herne\tMeneldir is in Herne, thinking deeply about the wight attack of the previous night.\n6\tFind Egfrith inside Crossway House\tMeneldir has not seen Egfrith since the wights attacked. Perhaps she returned to the inn?\n7\tEgfrith is missing. Perhaps one of the townspeople knows where she has gone.\t\n8\tFlip over the parchment Egfrith left with Aberthol\tEgfrith left a note for you and your companions. It lies face-down on Aberthol's table.\n9\tRead the words of Egfrith's letter\tEgfrith wrote you a letter, entrusting it with Aberthol.\n10\tTalk to Meneldir outside Crossway House in Herne\tMeneldir is outside Crossway House in the town of Herne.\n11\tCatch Egfrith south of Herne before she can escape\tEgfrith is likely to have hurried directly southward in order to avoid the difficult ford at Tharbad. You and your companions should try to prevent Egfrith from escaping as she makes for Isengard and her master Saruman.\n12\tTalk to Meneldir on the edge of Minhiriath\tMeneldir stands by the dirt path leading south into Minhiriath.\n13\tTalk to Boromir on the edge of Minhiriath\tBoromir stands by the dirt path leading south into Minhiriath.\n",
[2053]="70000682\n1\tTalk to Radagast the Brown\tRadagast the Brown dwells in seclusion within a tower in the ruins of Ost Guruth, the place the Eglain call home. Seek out his counsel. Gadaric and Hunulf Munce believe that your intentions are good and have provided you with the whereabouts of their most esteemed guest.\n",
[2054]="70041355\n1\tTalk to Ioron, the dancing man in Linhir\tIoron is south of Ingalad, in Linhir. The folk of Linhir are concerned for the safety of Ioron, who has been acting peculiarly for several hours.\n2\tTalk to Ioron in Linhir\tIoron is south of Ingalad, in Linhir. You have spoken with Ioron and he insists that the winds of hope are on the rise. Has he truly gone mad, as the people of Linhir suppose?\n3\tCollect Southron badges from Haradrim in Lebennin (total: 8)\030Collect Umbar badges from Corsairs in Lebennin (total: 8)\tCorsairs and Haradrim can be found throughout Lebennin. Ioron wants you to defeat Corsairs and Haradrim throughout Lebennin, bringing the badges of rank they carry to Thorongil outside Pelargir.\n4\tFind Thorongil outside Pelargir, in Lebennin\tThe man Ioron believed to be Thorongil may be approaching the gates of Pelargir, in Lebennin. Ioron asked you to find Thorongil, great hero of Gondor.\n5\tBring Southron and Umbar badges to Aragorn outside Pelargir\tThe man Ioron believed to be Thorongil is in fact Aragorn, son of Arathorn. Ioron asked you to find Thorongil, great hero of Gondor, and you have found him outside Pelargir.\n",
[2055]="70061C29\n1\tTalk to Meneldir by the edge of Minhiriath\tMeneldir stands on the road that runs into Minhiriath, contemplating Boromir's decision.\n2\tMeet up with Meneldir at the east gate of Herne\tMeneldir will meet you back at the east gate of Herne, where the two of you will continue your journey to find his friend Narndir.\n3\tTalk to Meneldir at the east gate of Herne\tMeneldir agreed to meet up with you at the north gate of Herne, where the two of you will continue your journey to find his friend Narndir.\n",
[2056]="70041354\n1\tAragorn makes ready to lead his forces into the port city of Pelargir and reclaim it from the Corsairs of Umbar. To participate in the battle, open the Epic Battles Panel and select 'Retaking Pelargir' from the menu. After you successfully complete the battle, you will be returned to the location from which you entered it.\t\n2\tTalk to Aragorn at his camp outside Pelargir\tAragorn is outside the city of Pelargir, and wishes to discuss the course of the battle with you.\n",
[2057]="70000679\n1\tCollect bog-moss from bog-prowler nests (total: 10)\tThe bog-prowlers wander in Haragmar, east of Ost Guruth. In order to learn what might be causing the corruption of the swamp, Radagast needs bits of moss from the nests of the bog-prowlers.\n2\tBring the bog-moss to Radagast the Brown\tRadagast waits in Ost Guruth, west of Haragmar. You should return to Radagast the Brown with the moss you collected.\n",
[2058]="70041353\n1\tTalk to Aragorn and storm Balakhôr's flagship, the Night-jewel\tAragorn is at his camp in Lebennin, outside the city of Pelargir. Aragorn is ready to put an end to Balakhôr the Scourge, and the threat of Umbar, once and for all.\n2\tTalk to Aragorn at his camp outside Pelargir\tAragorn is outside the city of Pelargir. You have driven Balakhôr away in shame, and the threat of Umbar is ended for now.\n",
[2059]="7000067E\n1\tDefeat wights in Haragmar (total: 15)\tWights can be found deeper in Haragmar, the southern reaches of the Red Swamp, east of Ost Guruth. Radagast sent you back into the swamp to defeat the wights that are fouling the land with their evil.\n2\tTalk to Radagast the Brown in Ost Guruth\tRadagast the Brown waits at the tower at the northern end of the main thoroughfare in Ost Guruth. You should return to Radagast the Brown with news of your battle with the wights of Haragmar.\n",
[2060]="7000017F\n1\tTalk to Saeradan at his cabin along the Greenway\tSaeradan is at his cabin north along the Greenway in Bree-land. Saeradan the Ranger might know where you should meet up with Radagast the Brown.\n2\tTalk to Candaith at his camp in the Lone-lands\tCandaith is at his camp in the Lone-lands. Saeradan does not know where exactly Radagast was bound when he left the Ranger's cabin. He suspects that Candaith, the Ranger who watches the Lone-lands, may have information on the Wizard's whereabouts.\n",
[2061]="70061CA1\n1\tTalk to Halbarad and go with him to search the keep\tHalbarad is at Gorwen's camp south of Dol Ernil, preparing to search the keep for both his missing Ranger and Meneldir.\n2\tTalk to Halbarad at Gorwen's camp south of Dol Ernil\tHalbarad is at Gorwen's camp south of Dol Ernil, mourning the loss of Meneldir and the escape of the Grey Fear.\n",
[2062]="70061CA2\n1\tContinue your adventures in the Lone-lands or the North Downs, and reach Level 32\tHalbarad believes that you will provide much help to the Dúnedain as you grow stronger and continue your adventures in the Lone-lands or the North Downs.\n2\tTalk to Candaith at his camp near the base of Weathertop\tHalbarad told you to meet with another of the Dúnedain, a Ranger named Candaith who camps by the base of Weathertop, in the Lone-lands.\n",
[2063]="70061CA3\n1\tTalk to Candaith and depart for Rivendell with haste\tCandaith has words of warning and advice for you before you depart on the last leg of your journey.\n2\tTalk to Elrond in his library\tElrond is in the library of his home in Imladris.\n",
[2064]="70042DB6\n1\tHaradrim fleeing in the direction of the town of Erynos, east and north of Aragorn's camp, must be defeated before they can bring word of his victory at Pelargir. Aragorn has asked you to find tracks left by terrified Haradrim near the town of Erynos.\t\n2\tHaradrim fleeing in the direction of the town of Erynos, east and north of Aragorn's camp, must be defeated before they can bring word of his victory at Pelargir. Aragorn has asked you to find tracks left by terrified Haradrim near the town of Erynos.\t\n3\tTalk to Thurineth at the gate of Erynos\tThurineth has some news for you at the gate of Erynos. You defeated several of the Haradrim that fled from Pelargir, and a woman has hailed you from the gate of Erynos.\n4\tTalk to the Haradrim Sorcerer near Erynos\tThurineth saw a Haradrim sorcerer creeping around the outer wall of the town of Erynos, and wanted you to defeat him before you leave.\n5\tTalk to Aragorn at the Camp of the Grey Host\tAragorn is at the Camp of the Grey Host, to the north-west of Pelargir. You have tracked down and defeated the Haradrim warriors that fled from Pelargir.\n",
[2065]="7001424B\n1\tFind Rókur and lend him your aid\030Find Útrygg and lend him your aid\tRókur and Útrygg are exploring Zelem-melek. They departed from the southern passage exiting the Twenty-first Hall, but from there no one knows where they went. Brogur has asked you to lend any assistance to the dwarves Rókur or Útrygg if you come across them while exploring Zelem-melek.\n2\tTalk to Brogur\tBrogur is in the Chamber of Leadership off the Twenty-first Hall, in Zelem-melek. You have protected an overzealous dwarf from defeat at the hands of an uruk scout, and should report now to Brogur.\n",
[2066]="70061C2A\n1\tTravel north along the Greenway in the direction of Bree-land\tMeneldir has asked you to continue northward along the Greenway in the direction of Bree-land.\n2\tTalk to Meneldir on the Greenway\tMeneldir has come to a halt on the Greenway.\n3\tMeneldir told you he felt eyes upon the two of you. Spies?\t\n4\tSearch the surrounding area with Meneldir\tWhat has Meneldir discovered?\n5\tLearn what Meneldir has discovered\tWhat has Meneldir discovered?\n6\tTalk to Meneldir by the body\tThe body of a Ranger lies in the brush.\n",
[2067]="700000FC\n1\tTalk to Mincham\tMincham can be found in his camp on the southern edge of the Fields of Fornost. Halbarad has asked you to speak with Mincham to learn if the Enemy has retaken the ruins of Fornost, the ancient capital of Arnor.\n",
[2068]="70025338\n1\tTalk to Frithgeir\tFrithgeir is in the library at Zudrugund. Corunir has asked you to speak with Frithgeir about Nár, in hopes that he can reveal the source of his friend's unexpected knowledge of the Grey Company's possible road.\n2\tExamine Cluttered Book-shelf\tFrithgeir has pointed out book-shelves in Zudrugund where Nár has spent time recently, at the shelves south-east of Frithgeir, surrounding an illuminated statue. You should investigate book-shelves where Nár has shown recent interest, hoping it will prove instructive.\n3\tTalk to Nár\tNár is somewhere within Zudrugund. You have searched the book-shelves pointed out to you by Frithgeir, but have learned little that seems relevant to Nár's mysterious knowledge of the Grey Company's intentions.\n4\tTalk to Corunir\tCorunir is in Zudrugund, the dwarf-hall in Thrór's Coomb. You have spoken to Nár about what you found in the book-shelves you were pointed to by Frithgeir, but have learned little of use. You should report of your efforts to Corunir.\n5\tTalk to Candaith\tCandaith is at a camp-site of the Grey Company in a grove of trees east of the Dunlending village of Lhanuch, in Nan Laeglin. Corunir has sent you to speak with Candaith to see if he has thought of a reason for Nár to have mentioned the Paths of the Dead.\n",
[2069]="70042DB7\n1\tAragorn has asked you to help the members of the Grey Company prepare to depart on the Corsair ships bound for Minas Tirith. Rangers at the Camp of the Grey Host have begun to perform Aragorn's tasks. Help them with their 'Black Sails' quests to fulfill his wishes.\t\n2\tTalk to Aragorn at the Camp of the Grey Host\tAragorn is at the Camp of the Grey Host, waiting for your report on the preparations of the Corsair ships.\n3\tTalk to Angbor at the Camp of the Grey Host\tAngbor the Fearless is at the Camp of the Grey Host, waiting to speak with you. Aragorn is ready to depart for Minas Tirith on the Corsair ships, and has asked you to travel overland with Angbor and his men to learn the state of the war.\n",
[2070]="70061C2B\n1\tExamine the body of Narndir\tThe body of Narndir lies off the road in Cardolan. What happened to this friend of Meneldir?\n2\tTalk to Meneldir by the body\tMeneldir stands by the body of his slain friend, filled with grief, anger, and confusion.\n3\tTravel to Sarn Ford and learn what transpired there\tWhat happened at the river-crossing of Sarn Ford to result in the death of Narndir, so far from his usual dwelling-place?\n4\tTalk to Halbarad at Sarn Ford\tThe Ranger Halbarad shouts commands to his kin at Sarn Ford.\n",
[2071]="70001790\n1\tDefeat Ongbúrz Orcs at Norbury Gates (total: 10)\030Defeat Wargs at Norbury Gates (total: 6)\tThe Norbury Gates lie to the north of Mincham's camp. Mincham believes the only way to determine the strength of the forces of Angmar within Fornost is to test the defences erected at its gates. He has asked you to slay Orcs and Wargs and bring him a report of the resistance there.\n2\tTalk to Mincham\tMincham can be found at his camp in the southern Fields of Fornost. The Ranger Mincham will need to hear your report regarding the defences at the gates of Fornost.\n",
[2072]="700000FD\n1\tTalk to Halbarad\tHalbarad can be found in Esteldín. Mincham beseeches you take the knowledge of Angmar's presence at Fornost to Halbarad.\n",
[2073]="70042DC7\n1\tDefeat Haradrim in Upper Lebennin (total: 10)\tThe road into Upper Lebennin passes through the port-city of Pelargir. Angbor has asked you to travel east into Upper Lebennin and to defeat many of the Haradrim there.\n2\tFind the entrance to the vale of Tumladen, in Upper Lebennin\tThe vale of Tumladen is in the northern reaches of Upper Lebennin. You have defeated many Haradrim in Upper Lebennin and should now find the vale of Tumladen.\n3\tTalk to White City Refugee\tMany refugees from elsewhere in Gondor can be found throughout the vale of Tumladen.\n4\tTalk to Angbor outside the entrance to the vale of Tumladen\tAngbor has come to the entrance to the vale of Tumladen. You have learned that folk have been evacuated from Minas Tirith, and the war is about to be joined. You should find Angbor and tell him what you have learned.\n5\tFind the Crossings of Erui, east of Tumladen\030Defeat Haradrim that threaten the Crossings of Erui (total: 6)\tAngbor wants you to travel east of Tumladen to the Crossings of Erui, and to defeat the Haradrim camped there.\n6\tTalk to Angbor on the small hill west of the Crossings of Erui\tAngbor keeps watch on a hill just to the west of the Crossings of Erui.\n",
[2074]="70061C30\n1\tTalk to Galasebdir to the north-east of Sarn Ford\030Talk to Nethúr to the south-east of Sarn Ford\030Collect Ranger caches not far from Sarn Ford (total: 3)\tRangers charged with the defence of Sarn Ford can use your assistance. Halbarad also requested that you recover a few caches of supplies from nearby, with which the Dúnedain will be able to restock Sarn Ford.\n2\tTalk to Meneldir at Sarn Ford\tMeneldir is at Sarn Ford, where he is helping his kin recover from the recent attack.\n3\tThe earth has been kicked up at several locations near Sarn Ford, and Meneldir thinks you should examine some of those piles of dirt. He has a suspicion that the black riders left something behind, as they did at Herne.\t\n4\tBring the skull-shaped token to Meneldir at Sarn Ford\tMeneldir's hunch proved accurate: the black riders left a token behind, and it likely drew the wights to Sarn Ford in the days following their attack.\n5\tBring the Ranger caches he requested to Halbarad at Sarn Ford\tHalbarad is overseeing the recovery of the Dúnedain following the black riders' attack on Sarn Ford. You retrieved a number of Ranger caches and should bring them to Halbarad.\n",
[2075]="700000FF\n1\tTalk to Dori or Hannar\tBoth Dori and Hannar should be found in Othrikar, which lies north of Esteldín. Halbarad told you that the Dwarves of Othrikar are good Longbeards who were put to task by the Dourhands for many years, though they have recently thrown off their yoke. Although they are still pressed by the Dourhands, Halbarad has asked you to bring them word of the Council of Esteldín.\n",
[2076]="70001802\n1\tFind Dori\tThe Dourhands' camp where Dori is being held is west of Othrikar. Search the ruins for where Dori is being held. Hannar told you that the dwarves could not even consider coming to the Council of Esteldín, unless Dori was freed from the Dourhands. As an envoy of the Rangers, he told you that you must free him if you hope to have the support of the dwarves at the Council. This quest is meant for a fellowship. If you choose to undertake this quest solo you will receive an inspiration bonus, but the challenge will be great.\n2\tTalk to Hannar\tHannar can be found at the mines of Othrikar. After escorting Dori to safety, he told you to return to Othrikar and speak to Hannar.\n",
[2077]="700000FE\n1\tTalk to Halbarad\tHalbarad can be found in Esteldín. Hannar told you to bring word to Halbarad that the Dwarves of Othrikar agreed to come to the Council.\n",
[2078]="70042DCE\n1\tFind the meeting of the roads just south of Imloth Melui, in Lossarnach\tAngbor has asked you to travel to the meeting of the roads just south of Imloth Melui, in Lossarnach, to learn the state of the war in that land.\n2\tTalk to Bandron on the road south of Imloth Melui\tBandron and Nethadan have stopped their waggon south of Imloth Melui, in Lossarnach, and you should find out what has brought them here and why they have stopped.\n3\tLook within the Harlond, near the entrance of the city\030Look within the Harlond, near the docks\030Look within the Harlond, near the gate of the Rammas Echor\tBandron has asked you to go to Harlond and look at certain locations to determine whether it is safe for him to go that way: the entrance of the city, the docks, and the gate in the Rammas Echor, the Pelennor's encircling wall.\n4\tTalk to Bandron on the road south of Imloth Melui\tBandron is by his waggon in Lossarnach, south of Imloth Melui. You have investigated the port of the Harlond and found that it is occupied by the enemy. Bandron will not be able to go that way.\n5\tTalk to Nethadan in Imloth Melui\tNethadan is somewhere within Imloth Melui, looking for a purchaser for the Cemenduril liquor.\n6\tTalk to Bandron on the road south of Imloth Melui\tBandron is on the road south of Imloth Melui, waiting for his son Nethadan to return.\n7\tTalk to Angbor on the road south of Imloth Melui\tAngbor is standing by Bandron's waggon on the road south of Imloth Melui, in Lossarnach.\n",
[2079]="70061C32\n1\tTalk to Halbarad and hear what befell the Rangers\tHalbarad is at Sarn Ford. Halbarad has agreed to tell you what befell the Rangers at Sarn Ford just days past.\n2\tTalk to Halbarad at Sarn Ford\tHalbarad is at Sarn Ford.\n",
[2080]="700000F7\n1\tTalk to Gildor Inglorion\tGildor Inglorion can be found in the Elf-glade of Lin Giliath, south of Esteldín. Halbarad told you that the Elf-glade was recently attacked by Stone-trolls. He expressed his concern that the Elves of Lin Giliath will be too overwhelmed dealing with the aftermath of this attack to come to the Council.\n",
})
